# Real places

When creating or improving a real location, follow `docs/place-authoring.md`.
Scans are primarily offline references for proportions, layout and elevation.
Identify the architecture and landmarks in photos, then author clean coherent
geometry, materials, gardens and collision for the game's established pixel style.
Do not present a raw scan with a pixel filter, posterization or patched floor as
finished art. Inspect both arrival framing and the player's walking route.
For example, Lourizán requires its glazed wings, mansard roofs, central clock,
paired staircases and terrace balustrades to remain recognizable.
Record source links, estimated dimensions and actual visual/physical validation.
